--
N5008 [temp.inst]/5 + [expr.const]: a void-returning constexpr member
function template never yields a constant, so it is deferred to the
method-body drain (whose prepare_deferred_method_body pack-expander
expands its std::construct_at-style new-initializer pack) rather than
eagerly converted before that expansion runs.  The C++20
allocator_traits::construct shape.  g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
